# November 28, 2026: state hospitals and asylums of Iowa, Missouri, Kansas and Nebraska, a batch of the themed pass on
# historic state hospitals. Osawatomie State Hospital and its Asylum Bridge, the Buchanan County Infirmary and the Lincoln
# veterans' hospital were already on the map and are not added again.
# Sources opened in this session: Wikipedia's articles on each institution and its list of Kirkbride Plan hospitals; the
# Kirkbride Buildings site; the Park Service's National Register records (St. Vincent's Hospital; the Nevada infirmary) and
# the Register form for the Beatrice institution's farm; the Missouri State Archives' online exhibit on the Fulton asylum;
# the Missouri Department of Mental Health's history pages; the St. Joseph Museums' hours page; the City of St. Louis
# preservation plan and Built St. Louis; the Buchanan County (Iowa) history site; the Kansas Preservation Alliance and the
# Topeka library's local history pages; the 1912 Kansas cyclopedia; and news reports (Associated Press, Southeast Iowa
# Union, Glenwood Opinion-Tribune, KJAN, Great Bend Tribune, Riverfront Times). Asylum Projects' pages were used only for
# dates and details nothing else gave, and the text says so. No patient is named. Pins: OpenStreetMap features, address
# lookups and Wikipedia's points, every one looked at on the aerial.
from data_b import N
from data_ma import W
BATCH={'key':'asylum_plns_mmxk','label':'State hospitals and asylums, Iowa, Missouri, Kansas and Nebraska','added':'2026-11-28 07:33'}
AP='https://asylumprojects.org/index.php/'
KB='https://www.kirkbridebuildings.com/buildings/'
